        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Corcovado and Christ the Redeemer"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0b9b0260533dc02c2cffb5f7d8eef978f025a7154fbcaf8dc78828979a6c402a",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-wm-p7lxhnqwgwc",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you'll set out on another four-hour tour.\n\nAt the station, you'll board an eco-friendly train that runs through the Tijuca Forest to the summit of Corcovado. The forest is home to monkeys, exotic birds and other wildlife.\n\nThe 38-metre Christ the Redeemer statue, built in 1931, stands at around 700 metres above sea level. From the viewing platform, you can see Rio and the surrounding area, including the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, Maracanã Stadium, Sugarloaf Mountain and the neighbourhoods between the mountains and the ocean. The train ride itself is part of the experience: dense tropical vegetation passes right outside the windows, with occasional glimpses of the city through the trees."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:b2f0e19acda78198",
